{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected control is assessed for one identified benefit offer by a distributor to a client in the SFC-authorised-fund setting.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A meaningful product association created by the manner of offering can suffice without product-specific gift eligibility.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Actual investor distraction is not a separate factual prerequisite; the stated purpose informs the linkage interpretation.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Gift and discount classifications are supplied judgments. The result flags only this selected control.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"1ec8bb5b62e8a4e2d2102a4deb5f614765043e712875cc812e04515fa91746c2","candidate_id":"candidate.b3c06ea9589e47d0b1888ebeb56c28fb","controlled_language":"Read 'offered in such a way that they are linked' as extending the control to indirect but meaningful promotional associations created by presentation or campaign design. A non-discount gift linked in that manner to a product or fund-house category falls within the selected control even when its eligibility terms are product-neutral. The fee-discount exception continues to apply.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.8836e0fb78c34f3d9cca8d0d8ec1cabf","issue.a9284a56d0044fd693102bb205927b69","issue.6be4a31eb57045ff8846edbf71e1f556","issue.ec8ee72b61df4c22bc6b5db88410517c"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"Reaches a meaningful association produced by campaign presentation as well as an express connection. In the account-opening-gift example in R1, contextual linkage to one fund house flags the non-discount gift even though eligibility is investment-neutral. This reading has stronger support in 'offered in such a way' and the distraction rationale, but the missing FAQ prevents settling how much contextual association suffices.","run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"7b78bffd5267abb04c58ab204d1e34f621dc3fb03008be1b35980abcaa535ba4","source_unit_ids":["u14","u30"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: contextual product connection"}